{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGramFactorisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGramFactorisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedBlockShiftTrace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NoncommRing","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.distSq_one_species","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.distSq_one_species","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ParticleGramFactorisation.lean#L137-L142","doc":"One species: every pair of distinct particles is at squared distance\n`2 (a - τ²)`, i.e. the particles form a regular simplex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.distSq_species","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.distSq_species","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ParticleGramFactorisation.lean#L127-L135","doc":"**Species law.**  If every off-diagonal entry factorises and the diagonal\nand one-point data depend only on a species label `s`, then two pairs of\ndistinct particles with the same species labels are at the same distance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.distSq_eq_of_factorised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.distSq_eq_of_factorised","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ParticleGramFactorisation.lean#L121-L125","doc":"If the off-diagonal entry factorises, the distance depends only on the\ndiagonal data and the one-point values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.distSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.distSq","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ParticleGramFactorisation.lean#L118-L119","doc":"Squared Gram distance `G i i + G j j - 2 G i j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.cov_eq_zero_of_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.cov_eq_zero_of_chain","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ParticleGramFactorisation.lean#L81-L110","doc":"**Bond locality (no next-nearest correlation).**  Let the nucleus bond element\nbe `P = Rᵗ M R` with the left bond part `M` below the cut (`H n`) and the right\nbond part `R`, `Rᵗ` above it (`shifted n`).  If the left particle `a ∈ H n`\ncommutes with `Rᵗ` (it is far from the right bond) and the right particle\n`b ∈ shifted n`, then `a` and `b` are uncorrelated in the state of `P`.  This is\nthe case of particles `0` and `2` of a chain `0 — 1 — 2` with bonds `B₀`, `B₁`,\n`P = B₁ᵗ B₀ᵗ B₀ B₁`, `M = B₀ᵗ B₀`, `R = B₁`, cut between the two bonds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.cov_eq_zero_of_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.cov_eq_zero_of_right","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ParticleGramFactorisation.lean#L74-L79","doc":"**Cut on the left.**  If `P` and the right particle live above the cut and the\nleft particle below it, the covariance vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.cov_eq_zero_of_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.cov_eq_zero_of_left","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ParticleGramFactorisation.lean#L66-L72","doc":"**Cut on the right.**  If the bond element `P` and the left particle `a` both\nlive below the cut (`H n`) and the right particle above it (`shifted n`), the\ncovariance vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.cov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.cov","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ParticleGramFactorisation.lean#L61-L64","doc":"Unnormalised covariance of `a`, `b` in the state `x ↦ tr (P x)` (up to `tr P`):\n`tr (a P b) tr P - tr (a P) tr (P b)`.  Dividing by `(tr P)²` gives the\ncovariance `⟨a, b⟩ - ⟨a, 1⟩⟨1, b⟩` of the probe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.connected_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ParticleGram.connected_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ParticleGramFactorisation.lean#L56-L59","doc":"On a braided tower, two particles on disjoint strand windows are uncorrelated. ","signatureChunk":0}]}